{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237899-describe-your-present-campaign-all-editions-equally-welcome","id":1237899,"title":"Describe Your Present Campaign (All Editions Equally Welcome)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-22T23:42:37-07:00","id":1237899,"title":"Describe Your Present Campaign (All Editions Equally Welcome)","content":"So,<br /> Was interested in the games my fellow fans are running. Would love to hear about the happenings in your games, wildest moments, favorite resolved/upcoming story arcs, characters/NPCs you're most proud of etc. All Editions Welcome, but if something you're describing hinges on something that others might not be up on, elaboration appreciated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I realized I'd been coming on a bit strong in some threads, so wanted to do something fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Since I started this, here goes:<br /> My present game is four years, ten months old. Mainly 2E. Game began in RY 768, and is presently in RY 914.<br /> The Cast:<br /> Davion Chance/Murr-ya Wyldwraith, Full Moon Lunar, Gallant, Motivation: Protect the Domain of the Eventide Pheonix and its people. Defend the Northeast of Creation. 368yrs Exalted, Essence 7<br /> <br /> Lireal Vendra, the Eventide Pheonix. Twilight Solar, Paragon, Motivation: Restore the Glories of the First Age, Protect and expand the Domain. 145yrs Exalted, Essence 6<br /> <br /> Viridian Strix, Heretic of the Razor's Edge. Slayer Infernal, Paragon, Motivation: Destroy every influence of the Yozis upon Creation, Urge (Malfean) Destroy the Greyfalls Dominion, 145yrs Exalted, Essence 6* (Note: Viridian Strix has mastered the Heretic Charm, Swallowing the Scorpion. He is believed to be the first true Heretic.)<br /> <br /> The Onyx Stiletto Rends All Life, AKA: Osral, Day Caste Abyssal, Conniver, Motivation: Cast the Mask of Winters into Oblivion, Annihilate the Duchy of Winter, Murder the other Deathlords like he murdered the Walker in Darkness. (Monstrance destroyed by detonation of R.I.D acquired from the Warrior-Smiths of Iza. Wanted throughout the Confederation of Rivers for Crimes against Humanity and Creation. Red Listed by the Bronze Faction Chair of the Committee on Entrenched Anathema.) 145yrs Exalted, Essence 6<br /> <br /> Eventide Seraph, Chosen of Secrets (Ronin), Architect, Motivation: Unearth secrets of the First Age, Prove or disprove veracity of the Theory of Historic Anathema Instability Syndrome. 388 years Exalted, Essence 7<br /> <br /> Timeline of notable events:<br /> RY 768: Remnants of Arczecht Horde flee northeast, ignoring Metetha. Cross the Sandy River, south of Cho-Holuth.<br /> Calibration of 768, Legions of the True Blooded Shogun besiege Sperimin, lead by the Daughters of Iza. Raksi's Ape-men and outlying cannibal tribes pushed back into the city before the month is out. Raksi summons Octavian to disperse invaders. Octavian battles noble warstrider-equipped unknown champion of Shogun's forces. Octavian gains the upper hand, but is forced to withdraw by concentrated shelling from Essence cannons brought to the fore during the &quot;duel.&quot; Raksi summons Gervisin to assist Octavian, but reinforcements continue to enter theater of conflict.<br /> Descending Water, 769: Sperimin completely encircled by Shogun's forces. Hundreds of First Circle Demons reinforce the ape-men defenders, but cordon continued to tighten.<br /> Resplendent Earth 14-21, 769: Marukani cavalry rides in support of Lookshyan expeditionary force, against Arczechti to prevent horde from crossing the Grey River. After heavy casualties, Arczechti disengage and turn northward. Lookshy and their Marukani allies read map, laugh maliciously, withdraw back across the Grey, and shadow the Arczechti to ensure Nexus's safety.<br /> Ascending Fire 16th, 769: Thousands of goat-wolf men detected by Shogun's forces approaching from Southeast, True Blooded air assets attempt to disperse beastmen, but find themselves engaged by a huge Strix, Steelbeak, and Warhawk, in addition to several elementals. True Blooded air assets withdraw with minor damage, after inflicting minor damage on advancing beastfolk horde. Shogun's reserve forces deployed to southeastern portion of cordon.<br /> Ascending Fire 16th, 769: Under cover of darkness, hundreds of Xaalite spider-folk infiltrate northeastern portion of True Blooded lines, as Sperimin Demons go on the offensive. Forewarned of the Lunars' plans, Xaalite spider-folk are slaughtered, many of Raksi's demons are banished or destroyed, and Xaal himself is gravely wounded and captured. Dark Eyes appears in the True Blooded war camp, claims Xaal, and carries the badly wounded Lunar away, even as Xaal damns him as a traitor.<br /> Ascending Fire 17th, an ear-splitting scream resounds throughout Sperimin, carrying miles beyond the besiegers lines. True Blooded air patrols spot the huge goat-wolf beastman horde withdrawing back the way they'd come.<br /> Midnight, Ascending Fire 17th, 769: Raksi appears atop the sorcerously fashioned earth-works surrounding the inner third of Sperimin's ruins, before the massed concentration of True Blooded forces to the Southeast. A great ball of green fire appears between her delicate hands, but something goes terribly wrong. Raksi is consumed by eldritch emerald flames, as the resultant shockwaves shatter the southern earthworks, killing hundreds of True Blooded legionaries. Ten Izan sorcerers give their lives diverting the devouring fire, saving the bulk of the southern cordon.<br /> <b>Lytek receives Raksi's Exaltation, finds it wiped utterly clean of memory. The Right Hand of Power sheds a single tear, for what might have been.</b><br /> <br /> The Shogun's forces mourn their dead for a full day, while the names of The Ten, as the sorcerers come to be called, are inscribed on the warstrider of the Shogun's Champion.<br /> Ascending Fire 19th, 769: The Legions of the True Blooded Shogun invest what remains of Sperimin, claiming <i>The Book of Three Circles. </i>Expert scavenger-teams are deployed with the remaining sorcerers to loot the city. By Descending Fire 10th, the little which remained of Sperimin is stripped bare. The Legions march north. Honoring their bargain with Dark Eyes, the loggers of Far Hold, man, woman, and child are put to the sword. Elder Oak is beaten savagely, clapped in <i>Manacles of Endless Night</i>, and imprisoned. The legions depart Farhold, leaving the tribes to loot the city under Dark Eyes.<br /> <br /> Ascending Fire 20th, Lireal Vendra Exalts as a Twilight in Halta's capitol, Chanta, treating cases of Green Sun sickness.<br /> Night of Ascending Fire 20th, Elements of Arczechti horde pillage and burn the town of Rainbright, despite the best efforts of its small guard. As his comrades stand and die, the son of their Captain and newest inductee breaks ranks, and flees into the night. Later that night, the Agatae <i>Ephemeral Sting</i> visits the remorse-wracked warrior. Viridian Strix accepts Malfeas's offer, Exalting as a Slayer on Ascending Fire 26th. His brother, town sneak-thief and ne'er-do-well, Stooping Direhawk, dying from an Arczechti lance in the gut, is visited by the Walker in Darkness. Exalts as a Day Caste the night of the 20th.<br /> <br /> Descending Fire 28th, 769: Eventide Seraph, having failed to convince Ayesha Uru that the sudden unraveling of the fates of Sperimin and Farhold are indicative of an event at least as significant as the Solar Return, defects from Heaven after two hundred and forty-three years faithful service to the Bureau of Destiny.<br /> <br /> Ascending Air 10th, RY 770: Xaal, recovered from his injuries, contacts his mentor Wyldwraith by Infallible Messenger. Details fall of Sperimin and Farhold, describing the unprecedented level of First Age technology possessed by the invaders, and Dark Eyes collusion. The older Lunar bestirs himself from the Argent Redoubt and goes to investigate.<br /> <br /> That was basically where everything began. I riffed off of the First Age Dragon Blooded Gen Iza, who Mercury instructed to gather up tons of disaffected and orphaned Terrestrials, pile up the resources, and depart into the Wyld. After creating a huge fiefdom out there (with the help of the Emanation of one VERY peculiar Unshaped), they were finally returning to Creation.<br /> <br /> So, anyone else?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","user":"Wyldwraith","date":". 07-23-2018, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T12:35:26-07:00","id":1238329,"title":"","content":"Out of interest, what XP level did you start at, and how do you handle such long downtimes? Since the game has been like 150 years.<br /> <br /> So, I play two games currently, both have been going at least 8 years, not sure exactly. One I used to run.<br /> <br /> I'll start with the other, the game of some of the most ineffectual Exalts ever. It's 8-10 years of game, so I'll try to make it readable.<br /> <br /> We started on the great steppe of Mon-Gul, in the north-west of the Scavenger Lands.<br /> We were investigating a ruin the Realm was also interested in, and we wanted to stop local Realm-aligned tyrant Timojin from uniting the tribes.<br /> We fought him and his army. They shot our Zenith warlord to death, and beat up my Twilight. So we flew away to another country before the Wyld Hunt arrived.<br /> We went to the river kingdom of Sukhmet, and investigated caves of magitech. But our Dawn got in a fight, flared, and died. So we flew north before the Wyld Hunt arrived.<br /> <br /> We arrived in the Haslanti League and were hired on an airship expedition to the West. While we were there, the teenage Night caste and teenage Changing Moon got drunk and ended up in bed. After that they started dating.<br /> <br /> The core characters by this point were:<br /> Meek Proudfoot, 15 year old Night Caste street kid from Sukhmet... with a panther familiar;<br /> Lysa Bloody-Claws, 16 year-old Changing Moon from the slums of Nexus;<br /> Shadow of Kings, Twilight sorcerer of the steppes;<br /> Cid Hawkwind, Twilight Haslanti airship engineer.<br /> Other PCs came in and out of the game.<br /> <br /> The expedition flew west, coming across a variety of strange islands where many sailors were killed by monsters, etc. The realm also sent a fleet, who we clashed with.<br /> <br /> We eventually reached an ancient Dragon King city, woke the sleepers, and crushed the Realm army.<br /> <br /> We then flew to Coral, but on the way Shadow of Kings accidentally blew up the airship, so we had to go on a raft. Slowly.<br /> <br /> In Coral, we joined a revolution that overthrew the government. We were largely ineffectual. Also, Lysa, now pregnant with Meek's kid, forced Meek to marry her.<br /> <br /> We stayed in Coral for a while, and then found an ancient manse that seemed to transport a consciousness es back a million years into the bodies of some Dragon Kings in Rathess. We explored the city, but when we tried to go through the gate to Yu-Shan, we woke up in our normal bodies in Harborhead.<br /> We helped rebels kick out their Autocthonian masters and free Harborhead. Then Ahlat asked us to come stay at his heavenly palace for a while.<br /> After about a month, Sukhmet, crocodile-god of Sukhmet, asked us to come help stop a war.<br /> <br /> We went to Sukhmet, now somehow moved to next to the Summer Mountains, and stopped a war with another country.<br /> However, Shadow of Kings lost all his Solar powers somehow. And his Raksha girlfriend was kidnapped. We investigated, and eventually discovered that the bad guy was... Shadow of Kings! He'd got sick of the party, replaced himself with a mortal clone, and gone off to become a mad, evil sorcerer.<br /> The circle defeated him, but he escaped.<br /> <br /> For the last few years, we've been protecting Sukhmet from threats internal and external: invasions, Dragon King cults (plural), an Abyssal, etc. Various Exalts have joined or left the party, some left and came back.<br /> Thanks to Lysa's political manoeuvres, Meek is now son/son-in-law of the recently deceased Pharoah.<br /> <br /> However, currently a Nephwrack and his cult are causing chaos, and in our efforts to defeat him, Meek and Khalum (another Night) stupidly released a horde of monsters and forbidden gods from beneath the earth. This also killed the Pharoah and all the county's exorcists, as well as tons of regular people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-24-2018, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T13:12:49-07:00","id":1238341,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sun Forged Oath is the tale of a group of extraordinary people living in the culturally diverse, and dangerous region of River Province. A loose confederation of City-states, Republics, and Kingdoms united in the cause of independence both political and financial from the monolithic Scarlet Empire. <br /> <br /> They will all be drawn into the world-shaking events of the Time of Tumult, forging their own destinies while up taking arms against the Enemies of Creation. <br /> <br /> Our story begins in the small township of <a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/wikis/tenyio\" target=\"_blank\">Tenyio</a>, a riverside trading port town filled secrets, wonders, and opportunities for adventure for those foolhardy enough to take the risks. </span></span></span><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/wikis/the-story-so-far\" target=\"_blank\">The Story So Far</a></b></span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T20:30:32-07:00","id":1238493,"title":"","content":"XP Level:<br /> The Full Moon and Chosen of Secrets (the Full Moon I ran as a quasi-NPC, as something of a safety net because I had two relatively new to Exalted players to begin. The Chosen of Secrets was the PC of my one veteran, and I just used the XP table in 2E Core for their respective ages. The age table builds, with the proportion requirements for what gets spent where is really very, very balanced IMO) I padded them both just a little, but then I simply didn't give them XP for awhile. My veteran was fine with that.<br /> <br /> Downtime was not as big as you might think. We tend to play three times a week, but more important is one of the major setting-pieces. Gen Iza built essentially their own Shogunate out in the Deep Wyld, and had eventually allied with the Autochtonians once the Locust Crusade stuff got done with. Izan agents had recovered Filial Wisdom, and brought him back to their territory. To limit my PCs from running off to the magitech-advanced civilization out in the Wyld to solve their problems, I installed an Unshaped across the Waypoints that must be trod to reach Shogunate territory. Shatters Infinity With the Hourglass was promise-bound not to use it's time-flow-manipulating abilities in a destructive manner versus the True Blooded Shogunate and Shogunate natives, but it was only constrained from active hostilities against non-natives bearing passage-tokens. (The Unshaped was not so much an &quot;ally&quot; as a non-enemy who provided minimal assistance to the Shogunate in exchange for a safe harbor to scurry into if a Haanya pack came unusually shallow. In my campaign, it was cosmologically understood the &quot;Traditional&quot; Unshaped had abandoned &quot;Pure Chaos proper&quot; for the border-edge of Deep Wyld and Pure Chaos. The Haanya preferred to stay to the &quot;middle&quot; and further out into Pure Chaos, but the more complex Unshaped could tolerate the &quot;shallower&quot; portion of Pure Chaos, and even the &quot;deeper&quot; Deep Wyld without discomfort. Whereas a Haanya in the Deep Wyld was akin to a a killer whale surfing up the beach for seals. In any case, the Unshaped wanted to continue existing a great deal more than they wanted to wipe out the irritating chunk of metaphysical grit the Shogunate's 25-ish Waypoints represented.<br /> <br /> Time distortions INVARIABLY nailed the PCs both coming and going. I had been of the opinion the first time the PCs lost twenty-four months, relatively easy access to two-dot and very very expensive three-dot magitech would lose a lot of its luster. Especially since I was merciless about their enemies advancing plans in their absence. Instead, my PCs simply learned to adapt to enemies who now had tons of prep-time. I tried widening the time-differential once, costing the PCs an outright twenty-five years, but the general consensus was (Out of Character) that once was novel, repeats would kill their connection with their own agendas in Creation. I also decided I didn't really care for the extensive book-keeping on &quot;lived versus actual&quot; time Exalted I'd have had to keep, since we were nearing the beyond-a-mortal lifespan mark than denotes de-gating higher Essence. (Which, BTW, I do not treat as anything REMOTELY as easy as navel-gazing for six months like Core describes) I keep the age-limits, but it's Beyond Epic Enlightenment Quest-level if you want to exceed Essence 5.<br /> <br /> There was also the factor the Domain of the Eventide Phoenix was located north-northeast of Halta, while getting into the Shogunate required heading into the deep Southeast, negotiating (later sometimes fighting past) the Opal Court, and then slogging through three Waypoints of Bordermarches, 1-6 Waypoints of Middlemarches, and 1-6 Waypoints of Deep Wyld, just to reach the Waypoints that made up the Shatterer (who the PCs eventually proved clever enough to begin propitiating). Travel was a big, big thing for the first three years. Obviously, increasing PC power-levels lead to faster travel...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T20:36:44-07:00","id":1238495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237899-describe-your-present-campaign-all-editions-equally-welcome?p=1238493#post1238493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We tend to play three times a week</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh to have that much free time again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T22:38:20-07:00","id":1238517,"title":"","content":"I'm running a Play-by-Post 3rd Edition campaign over on the GitP forums, titled The Lotus Blossoms! (exclamation point included). It started as a martial-arts-themed attempt to homage shounen anime, but quickly bloomed into something messier and more fun. I think the most succinct way to describe it is that by the end of the first in-game day my players found a way to restructure the government of a nation <i>none of them have even visited</i>.<br /> <br /> The PCs are...<br /> <br /> Brown Leaf, Zenith Caste. Ex-Immaculate from rural Harborhead. Very good at smashing things. Trying to get better at putting them back together. Tiger stylist.<br /> Ivory Knife, Eclipse Caste. Habitual social manipulator, aspiring leader of an anti-Realm insurgency. Silver-Voiced Nightingale / Black Claw stylist.<br /> Tuoni, Twilight Caste. Blank-masked Linowan shaman. Often plays the &quot;exasperated parent&quot; role to the rest of the party. Crane / White Reaper stylist.<br /> Wirric Stanton, Twilight Caste. Alchemist, sorcerer, Guildsman, and self-proclaimed villain, originally from Whitewall. Righteous Devil stylist.<br /> Slang, Night Caste. Tya ship's captain, storm-chaser, and survivalist. Snake stylist.<br /> <br /> Collectively, they're meandering in the general direction of chasing down a rogue Gold Faction Sidereal who's trying to weaponize other Solars, but not before murdering a king, falling in love with an Abyssal, starting a Limit-Break-fueled gang war in Champoor, permanently killing a god, and fishing one of Ma-Ha-Suchi's lieutenants out of a sea of improbabilities.<br /> <br /> It's the best group of players I've ever GMed for, and the best game of Exalted I've ever been involved with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-24T23:59:36-07:00","id":1238525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Megapope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237899-describe-your-present-campaign-all-editions-equally-welcome?p=1238495#post1238495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahhh to have that much free time again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, yeah. We play once a month. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (We actually play 3-4 different games, and cycle through them weekly, because none of the STs can run every week. Plus, years ago when we were students we did play multiple games per week, and we don't want to end some of those. I'd rather run more than once a month, but there's no time.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T02:50:17-07:00","id":1238540,"title":"","content":"We've got a two games on the go, as we play weekly but switch up stories every 3 months or so:<br /> <br /> <u>SMASH THE REALM!</u><br /> <br /> 4 solars, including a 9ft tall barbarian Dawn Caste, a battle sorcerer Twilight and two new characters I can't remember (because we got ambushed and the old characters died) are running a guerilla war against the realm, repeatedly hitting supply lines and small outposts. When the next chapter starts, we will mostly be running away from the two legions sent to hunt us down until we can ambush <i>them</i>.<br /> <br /> <u>The Grand Tour</u><br /> <br /> Five 21 year old guys, fresh out of secondary school head out on their gap year. About to get in way above their head while dealing with lunar sponsored &quot;bandits&quot; outside An Teng,<ul><li>Fire aspected swordsman from House Cathak, aiming to be such a great general he's allowed to marry within the house and so gets to stay in the Cathak legions. Keeps helping out a government-backed assassin and is having moral issues about it so I'm not sure why he keeps doing it...</li> <li>Air aspected archer from house Mnemon who hates his cousin who is the Satrap of An Teng (but I think doesn't know why yet). Will literally do nearly anything to undermine him, and the feeling is mutual.</li> <li>Earth aspected sorcerer from house Mnemon, who only really cares about promoting himself as a sorcerer and ingratiating himself into posh society through the use of large sums of money and finding up and coming artists.</li> <li>Water aspected &quot;gentleman thief&quot; from house Ledaal, who can't handle his drink but can't stop going to parties and has got tangled up with an Abyssal who took advantage of his love for pretty ladies and has just stolen something from the palace for her...</li> <li>Wood aspected healer from house Peleps, who spends most of his time making drugs, poisons and hangover cures, practicing his comedy routine, and convincing the water aspect to test his latest batches.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T04:13:59-07:00","id":1238548,"title":"","content":"Right now, we're at the tail end of a Solar vs Mask of Winters story for Exalted first-timers, with little knowledge of the setting. Basically, thanks to an Illuminated Mentor, they caught wind of a conspiracy that was planning to &quot;level&quot; Lookshy and trigger a war inside the River Provinces.<br /> In the background, the Mask abused Lookshy's surprise to move North, and things degenerated in a protracted campaign.<br /> <br /> As things moved on, they realized the Lover had dispatched agents on missions beneficial to the Mask (securing Manses and towns). Things have come to a head when a think-tank of the Provinces contracted the Solars - they would be provided a ship and authorizations to enter Thorns. Their job was to fuck things as immensely as possible to force the Mask to fall back or risk losing his supply lines.<br /> <br /> So, they've been in Thorns a couple weeks now and have:<ul><li>Blown up an Abyssal disease research center, killing two Abyssals and multiple city guards</li> <li>Met and allied the local rebellion, whose leader has just received the Exigence of the dying city-father of Thorns.</li> <li>Murdered and replaced a noblewoman allied to the rebellion, because she was selling out orphans to ghosts. They have yet to mention that entire story to the rebellion.</li> <li>Met the Mask himself in parlay, who offered them to let them chose a replacement for the Autocrat as long as he kept the fealty of the new leader and as long as the Lover's ambassador was killed in a way that did not implicate him.</li> <li>Met the aformentionned ambassador, who admitted the Lover had masterminded the attack on Lookshy to force the Mask in a weakened situation. He is currently planning to overthrow the Autocrat and then threaten the Mask into leaving the city. Strangely, he does not seem to want to KEEP the city, which makes the PCs horribly nervous.</li> <li>They are now planning a massive coup with the ambassador and the rebellion during an upcoming opera, hoping to turn into a full-fledged rebellion.</li> <li>They have also just uncovered a few First Age documents they stole &quot;just in case&quot;</li> <li>They are also starting to worry that the think-tank may overrule their deals, or even try to backstab them when the Mask flounders.</li> </ul>Considering no player is reading this forum, here's the backstage: The Lover and the Mask were in life part of a group that researched extreme life-extension techniques. In death agreed to a deal: access to some of the Mask's research in exchange for her supporting his military expansion. So, she planned the entire Lookshy incident to go off too early for the Mask to be ready, spreading his forces thin. When her ambassador came to collect, he started the second phase: oust the Mask from the city where his Manse and research were located in life, ensuring that the Lover had the most immediate access to their First Age research on life-extension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T04:51:50-07:00","id":1238555,"title":"","content":"Alrighty.<br /> <br /> Currently I'm running a game called &quot;Immortals of Stone and Sacrifice&quot;.<br /> It concerns a city at the edge of the civilised world, fittingly dubbed Exile. Here, thousands of different cultures mix together in a m\u00e9lange of tongues and customs.<br /> <br /> Into this mix? Throw five Solars.<br /> We have:<ul><li>A Nexan mercenary captain, named &quot;Wolf of Veiled Vengence&quot;, who is a womanizing scoundrel, trying to forget the fact that his bonded mate is a monstrous pantherlady with an appertite for human flesh. He's the Dawn, although he behaves like a Night Caste in a lot of ways.</li> <li>A Vanehan ronin, on the run from the Sword Prince and the Clans that he spited. Hachidori is a Night Caste swordsmaster, practicing the Single Point Shining in the Void, and uses both Ride charms and Athlethics. Yet, his keen Investigation skills has made him the Magistrate of Exile.</li> <li>A young woman from the Air People with a talent for engineering, Silver Wisp is the Twilight of the group. She's the henmother-like inventor, quite ditzy, but scary comptent at times. And insecure as all hell, as she doubts that she is even worthy of being a Solar.</li> <li>A former monk turned beggar, Indomitable Boar is of immense girth and even grander insight into the ways of the world. He was once an Immaculate Acolyte, but his master casts him aside, and the Zenith Caste became far greater than his master ever was. Integrity is the core of this one's being, and he strives to bring his Circle to their destined mastery of all there is.</li> <li>A plantation owner and Guild Merchant, Aliyah was originally a courtier in Great Forks, but was sent packing due to a scandal. She fled with the wealth of her family, but finally Exalted when she tricked a Demon into giving her audience with Mara, The Shadow-Lover. Today, she seems like a benevolent and endearing young lady, but the will of iron and ruthlessness is hidden beneath her Black Claw style and Socialize charms.</li> </ul>And, well.<br /> They're doing a lot of stuff.<br /> <br /> To recap.<br /> The circle came together in several adventures, almost all of them centering around the machinations of Indomitable Boar who wanted to bring them together.<br /> They then formed a Circle, and stopped a soulsteel-clad juggernaut from claiming a place of power, by dropping the entire fortress atop of said juggernaut.<br /> <br /> After finding a immense Manse capable of drifting on the Dragon Lines, The Circle defeated a horde of wicked godeating Beastmen who were ravaging the spirit courts of the countryside. But, there was still a single godblooded daughter of a slain forest god missing, perhaps she could tell them why these Godeaters had been so successful.<br /> Following that, they attempted to place the city under their influence, but realized that such a chaotic city needed a firmer hand. Especially when a Deathknight known as the Scarlet Balladeer arrived with his harrowing music, almost sending the entire city into a black depression.<br /> Unable to kill the Deathknight, but strong enough to chase him away, the Solars tried figure out who had sponsored the Godeater Hordes, and sought out a ruined city at the edge of a collossal shadowland.<br /> Here, they discovered that the area had once been the staging ground for a rebellion against the Exalted by the Terrestial Gods, and five weapons had been forged to help the gods overcome the Solars in particular. Each blade meant for a individual caste.<br /> At this point, every clue they discovered pointed the Circle at the Deathknights as the hand behind the Godeaters. They've wanted to lay claim to another old Artifact from the Divine Revolution, a Crown meant to control a behemoth large enough to swat mountains like flies. Now, as the behemoth had been slain in the First Age, the Crown of Maggots could bring the creature back to unlife and serve as the Abyssals tool. The crown had been split apart, scattered to three different places in the region.<br /> The fortress that the Circle had encountered the juggernaut-like deathknight, He Who Sows Fear and Reaps Despair, had been one place.<br /> The god-ruled city of Moku was another.<br /> And finally, the last piece was hidden in the Changeling-ruled Kingdom of Blossoms.<br /> <br /> When the circle returned to Exile, they found that a messenger had arrived with a call for aid from the Kingdom of Blossoms. The Kingdom's own calender had stopped in the middle of their biannual Calibration, leaving the Kingdom in the hands of the madness-bringing Calibration King. (Think a Dementation-fuel Sidereal...)<br /> Through many trials, the Circle managed to put things right, but not before Limit Breaks ended up nearly tearing the Circle apart and the Day Caste known as Sanguine Scorn managed to pilfer the third piece of the Crown.<br /> <br /> From the Kingdom, they once more returned to their own city, and Aliyah solidified her hold, making her the High Despot of Exile, while the rest of the Circle began preparations of their own. Finally, they decided to embark on a quest to Moku, the City of Eternal Spring, where they saw what wonders a city ruled by unhindered Gods could be. Even though it was hedonistic and debauched, culture and craftsmanship thrived here.<br /> In Moku, they learned of the city's defenders, four powerful entities armed with the Sunkiller Blades, to secure Moku from Solar dominion. In Moku, they navigated politics of both Gods and the diplomats send by the Lunar Elder Raksi. Here, Wolf met his bonded mate again, and nothing was settled except more aches, as the machinations of Sanguine Scorn used the feuding as a cover for her theft of the third piece of the Crown.<br /> <br /> Enraged that they had been tricked, the Solars did manage to find certain clues to the identity of the Dusk Caste, He Who Reaps, and the composition of his seemingly impenetrable armor, and to do so, they continued into the wastelands of the north, to the City of the One-Eyed.<br /> Here, they found the knowledge they sought, and managed to get an ally in the form of the One-Eyed King, a mortal who fused with a shard of the Balorian Eye.<br /> <br /> Having gathered their allies in Exile, the Circle is now nearing Calibration, where a prophecy claims that the Brobdingnagian Worm will rise in the Canyon of Shadows. They march to face the Deathknights, and whoever those deathknights serve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T05:17:26-07:00","id":1238559,"title":"","content":"I have just begun a short-term game (no more than six sessions) using Exalted 2nd, Scroll of Errata, the Wyld and Graceful, Wicked Masques. All the player characters are rakshas. I will include more information as the game progresses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T05:39:40-07:00","id":1238562,"title":"","content":"I just ... really want to know how that Shadow of Kings reveal went down from the player side of things. Like, did his player play the mortal clone for a while? Was everyone in on it? Who came up with the idea? I'm just really interested in the logistics of mindfuckery in games because it's great fun but takes a lot of player trust to pull off. You have to get a certain amount of buy-in without spoiling too many things.<br /> <br /> Speaking of mind games ...<br /> <br /> My campaign has been going for over three years now. It's 2.5 edition with some minor rules tweaks. The setting is a homebrew modern shard, and the PCs are (or were) all Abyssals. <br /> <br /> I've gotta say, I've really enjoyed playing with Exalted in a modern setting. This is a world where the Meteorological Bureau retains political analysts to report on conflicts in the elemental courts. Where daring mortal hackers trap data spirits in yasal-drives and use their powers to get past the magical firewalls of dragonblood-run companies. Where satellites orbit the axis mundi, just below the ever-turning wheel of the constellations. Where a gang of street-ninjas runs illegal drugs (promising an easy path to enlightenment) from the back room of Thanh's Tengese Takeout in downtown Nexus. <br /> <br /> This is a world where the dragonblooded rule through corporations, courts, and every sort of political system from dictatorship to democracy to hold-out monarchy. Where Lunars are rumours, and Sidereals aren't even that. Where Solars haven't been seen or heard for a thousand years, passing from public consciousness to be remembered mostly by religious scholars as an allegory for humanity's hubris. <br /> <br /> The world's two superpowers are the Realm Eternal, occupying the Blessed Isle and a few tributary states, and the United Protectorates of the River Province (UPRP), occupying the central East. Both are successor states to the Shogunate which collapsed under its own weight after years of infighting and bureaucratic ineptitude hundreds of years ago. As it broke up, leading to the patchwork of nation states that exist in modern times, technology advanced to fill the gaps left by slowly failing First Age infrastructure. There was no Great Contagion, no Balorian Crusade, no apocalyptic event to cast humanity into a Dark Age. Not one that humanity remembers, anyway. <br /> <br /> The other entity that might be considered a great power is the Wyld Hunt, which in this world is a secular organisation focused on combating supernatural threats to Creation. It works with national governments through the League of Nations to co-ordinate responses to these threats and provide expert support to their military and police forces. It has a permanent force in each Direction roughly equivalent to the military of a small nation, plus a large list of reservists and volunteers who might be activated to assist with a crisis. <br /> <br /> The League of Nations has another military arm, the Iron Shield, an international military effort to keep threats from the Wyld away from the civilised lands of Creation by patrolling the borders of reality. <br /> <br /> Into this world, quite unexpectedly, in the Calibration between 767 and 768, strange new exalts started appearing. They weren't even sure they were exalts at first, because after all, that word was synonymous with dragonblooded, wasn't it? Every one of them had experienced something that should have killed them, only to wake up strong, vital, and brimming with dark essence. No deathlord offered them a bargain, no liege commanded them. But across the world, a handful of Abyssals nonetheless came into their power. Wisely, they tried to keep their power hidden from the authorities which would no doubt brand them dangerous. And they were dangerous. Some of them heard nonsensical whispers in their minds that nevertheless sometimes revealed horrible truths. All them found that their new natures demanded they align themselves with the power of death to an extent, lest their very essence rebel and produce spectral phenomena that might give them away, or overwhelm their minds with madness. But each of them was also a person with their own ambitions, their own morals, and their own heroic will, determined to make <i>something</i> of their new gifts, even in the absence of guidance. <br /> <br /> At the time, only a few scholars marked the fall of several Sentinel Stars, the bright lights that remained fixed in place in the night sky while all the other stars turned. But this phenomena lent the story its name ... <u><b>Starfall</b></u>. <br /> <br /> <b>The PCs</b>:<br /> <i><b>Besserack Cardun</b></i>: A teenage Day caste Abyssal from An-Teng. The son of a noble family that got shafted in its business dealings and was gutted by corruption charges and scandal. He died starving in a gutter (turns out being a rich kid doesn't prepare you well for homelessness). He has a familiar, the ghost of a rat that choked to death nibbling on his un-moving body as he lay dying. He started out pretty much just wanting to watch the world burn (especially the other rich families that screwed his over), but over time has developed more constructive ambitions, including overhauling the political system of An-Teng and finding a way to destroy soulsteel to free the souls inside (both still works in progress). He has few scruples, but to the relief of his circle-mates one of them appears to be loyalty. In addition to being sneaky, he is also devilishly persuasive. He is also a maker of fine poisons. He's pretty intellectual for a death-ninja, and has branched into thaumaturgy and artifact crafting recently. <br /> <br /> <i><b>Betahl Altensand-Berg</b></i>: A Dawn (former Dusk) caste from the Delzhan Republic. The daughter of a junkie mother and an absent father (Delzhan Army Lieutenant, MIA). She died in a cage fighting match against a dragonblood after refusing to go down in a previous match when instructed to by her crimelord boss. She got up and beat the other exalt senseless before stumbling home with her prize money. Her girlfriend broke up with her in the immediate aftermath of the match and she spent a lot of time wishing to be rid of her 'curse' while also reveling in her newfound power. She found her way to the Chiaroscuro criminal underworld and started taking odd jobs before meeting up with the PCs. As the game progressed she found her direction in life and came into her own as a champion against the (other) powers of darkness. She cleaned herself up, started a military career, and eventually redeemed into a Solar. Mostly fights with her fists. She is also a very accomplished sorceress specialising in defensive and war magic. <br /> <br /> <i><b>Kaiwa Valko (nee Shiruba)</b></i>: A former PC as the player left the game last year. Midnight caste from Chiaroscuro, in the Delzhan Republic. Lieutenant Shiruba Kaiwa was a Wyld Hunt specialist, the face of her special forces fang. She died on a diplomatic mission to the Realm when a dragonblooded diplomat grew enraged and attacked her. Her fang covered for her after she killed the diplomat, and she was quietly retired from the Hunt. She ran an underground organisation aimed at overthrowing dragonblooded hegemony and putting more power in the hands of mortals. While she retains this goal as a focus, she has also taken on the tasks of learning as much as she can about the various threats to Creation at large, in order to combat them, and of building connections to help the group achieve its goals. She has an obsessive personality, and an arrogant, abrasive demeanour when she's not trying to butter people up, but would do anything for the few people she lets close. Very persuasive, specialised in breaking through brainwashing. Over time, she has become an incredible teacher and multidisciplinary researcher. <br /> <br /> <i><b>Reynard Fox</b></i>: A Twilight (former Daybreak) caste from the streets of Nexus. He was a sorcerer-detective who died after chasing a suspect onto a roof and losing his footing (with a little help from an Air Aspect hurling lightning at him). Fox joined the game later, when the PCs were already established as a taskforce. He has a familiar, a fox spirit called Zorro, who is a little innocent ray of sunshine in a dark world. Fox's life has been plagued by a bad case of Sidereals, as he was once fated to receive the exaltation of Chejop Kejak after the elder Chosen of Secrets passing. That obviously didn't work out. After finding out about the existence of Sidereals he spent a lot of time resenting their influence on his life, but has made peace with it over time. After his knack for investigation and his powerful sorcery, Fox's greatest gift is sarcasm. <br /> <br /> <i><b>Dr Ashyria Jaya D'Mophry</b></i>: A Daybreak caste from the upper crust of Nexus society. Jaya (she goes by her middle name most of the time) also joined later in the campaign. She escaped the stifling world of Nexan high society by studying medicine and volunteering with an aid organisation in Halta. The Realm Eternal and the UPRP were having a proxy-war in the region, backing Linowan and Halta respectively, and she was unhappy with the way foreign interference was affecting the people and landscape of Halta, so she joined a group of rebels resisting the exploitation of their country. She died in an ambush set by a corrupt general. She has used the connections she has made over the course of the game to bring an end to the war (if not the animosity) and curtail her country's interference in Halta. She is blunt and straightforward (really, she made a terrible socialite), but an excellent healer (with access to Solar healing Charms), markswoman, and wilderness survivor. <br /> <br /> I'm going to save the story so far for a later post, because I should go eat and be productive, but here's a teaser in the form of a poem that haunted the PCs during Act One of the campaign:<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>Hell stands empty, the demons have fled<br /> The world is embraced by the souls of the dead<br /> The imprisoned princes have all ceased to be<br /> We killed them and killed them until they were free</i><br /> </div> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><i>Now maddened they clamour, in sight of their goal<br /> The ancients come back for the world that you stole<br /> Those traitors in Heaven can't forestall your fates<br /> It's the gods you forgot who now batter your gates</i><br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"center\"><i>Heaven still reeled from the first awesome blow<br /> When the stars conferred with the darkness below<br /> For the grim task at hand only souls would suffice<br /> For the sake of Creation they brokered a price</i></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T10:00:15-07:00","id":1238615,"title":"","content":"Some cool names there, Growls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237899-describe-your-present-campaign-all-editions-equally-welcome?p=1238562#post1238562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just ... really want to know how that Shadow of Kings reveal went down from the player side of things. Like, did his player play the mortal clone for a while?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I was playing a mortal. And not even an enlightened mortal.* Not even sorcery or supernatural martial arts.<br /> In a 500xp Celestial game.<br /> It was a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> *Later Cid, the other Twilight, enlightened him with a charm. And after defeating Shadow of Kings, the clone exalted as a Lunar. I played that Lunar for the next 3 or 4 years, but he got amnesia from shapeshifting without tattoos just before we switched to 3rd ed, so now he's gone off to learn from the Silver Pact and hopefully get his mutations and mind healed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Was everyone in on it? </div> </div> </div>No, none of us knew what was going on until we found Shadow of Kings in his lair.<br /> <br /> (Well, IIRC the ST told me 5 minutes before we met him so I could roleplay him. This was 3-6 years ago, so I don't remember exactly)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who came up with the idea? </div> </div> </div>I told my ST something like &quot;I've been playing Shadow of Kings for about 5 years, and I'm sick and tired of him. Could you do something interesting with him? Kill him dramatically, have him kidnapped by Yozis and turned into an Akuma, lose his powers, be turned into an Abyssal, whatever. I don't know, just something to change him because I'm bored. But I don't want him to just wander off, the other PCs wouldn't let him go.&quot;<br /> And he said &quot;Hmmmm... I had this one plot idea... let me handle it.&quot;<br /> Soon afterwards, I appeared to lose all my Solar powers. Also, we later discovered that my entire body had tiny orichalcum threads through it (because I was an artificial being). Also, my memories of the recent past became kind of fuzzy.<br /> It was a really good plotline, I really enjoyed it, but probably it wouldn't be to every player's taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-25-2018, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T10:44:28-07:00","id":1238625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1237899-describe-your-present-campaign-all-editions-equally-welcome?p=1238615#post1238615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, none of us knew what was going on until we found Shadow of Kings in his lair.<br /> <br /> (Well, IIRC the ST told me 5 minutes before we met him so I could roleplay him. This was 3-6 years ago, so I don't remember exactly)<br /> <br /> <br /> I told my ST something like &quot;I've been playing Shadow of Kings for about 5 years, and I'm sick and tired of him. Could you do something interesting with him? Kill him dramatically, have him kidnapped by Yozis and turned into an Akuma, lose his powers, be turned into an Abyssal, whatever. I don't know, just something to change him because I'm bored. But I don't want him to just wander off, the other PCs wouldn't let him go.&quot;<br /> And he said &quot;Hmmmm... I had this one plot idea... let me handle it.&quot;<br /> Soon afterwards, I appeared to lose all my Solar powers. Also, we later discovered that my entire body had tiny orichalcum threads through it (because I was an artificial being). Also, my memories of the recent past became kind of fuzzy.<br /> It was a really good plotline, I really enjoyed it, but probably it wouldn't be to every player's taste.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's awesome. I actually did something similar in a superhero game my non-exalted group played earlier this year, but at character creation. I played a character with amnesia who was very bad at human. I told the GM &quot;She doesn't know what happened to her or where her powers came from. She's been told who she was before, but she doesn't feel like she's the original, just something else that replaced her. Do what you like with that, let me discover it in play.&quot; It was great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T12:42:44-07:00","id":1238662,"title":"","content":"One thing I've really enjoyed about Storytelling for our present game, is its the first time I've had a group really want to &quot;go the distance&quot; with the same group of PCs. Everyone really seemed to dig in and get invested in the character they were playing, and anyone who plays much Exalted knows how rare it is for four people to all decide at the same time they're in love with their characters. Ironically, it was the Infernal that started it. Everyone got so invested in how Jacob roleplayed his break with Ligier, subsequent struggle to break away and forge a new and independent persona after being Hell's darling for so long (I didn't have Ligier get all wrathful and send death-squads or anything boring when Viridian Strix told him to fuck off, he wasn't killing anymore innocent people, and he understood why all of reality had risen up to throw the world's makers into prison. Instead, every time that things got tough, there was one of Ligier's agents, offering to grease the skids and ice the roads. The relapse-pull away cycle went on for awhile...until the other PCs sort of staged an intervention, and really got serious about helping Viridian Strix &quot;stay clean.&quot;)<br /> <br /> It wasn't until Strix had about five-six months where he'd stayed completely away from demonic influences, that he was able to realize just how much of his difficulties in staying out of Hell's hands were due to the carefully-placed insinuations and doubt-farming of his unwoven coadjutor. I know this might seem obvious, but I'd cultivated this &quot;No, I'm not on Hell's side. I'm on your side, dummy&quot; persona in the Agatae <i>Ephemeral Sting</i> coadjutor (Yes, I KNOW that unwoven coadjutors are supposed to be First Circle Demons descended from the Infernals Yozi, but I'd long since house-ruled it that it EITHER had to be a demon descendant of the Caste-Yozi, OR the Infernal had to take their Yozi's Urge. Some people might think a Slayer-Malfean Urge is a killbot, but not when done well.)<br /> <br /> Anyways, by playing up to Viridian Strix as being on his side first and foremost, <i>Ephemeral Sting</i> had broken down Strix's natural suspicions and conviction that the demon was on the side of Hell. It was really long-game work here, but it broke down in the face of the party keeping Strix away from Hell in much the same way as concerned family members or friends might work hard to keep a junkie from slipping off to score a fix. <i>Ephemeral Sting </i>got a little more obvious as its desperation built, and...finally, Strix twigged to the fact his unwoven coadjutor had been deeply-truly playing him like a fiddle. It was beautifully, beautifully done, and the pendulum swinging between righteous indignation and raw anguished betrayal ...if I could've given Jacob the Academy Award, I would've. As it was, he was scoring the bonus XP point nearly every session by group-consensus. Now, you might think THAT's where his whole &quot;I'm going Heretic&quot; began, and in a way that's where the motivation began, but there was no cheesing knowledge of Infernal Heresy into existence. Strix really started digging deep for options in how to make a permanent break with Hell. Exploring leads indicated by knowledge his Past Life possessed, and there were so very many entertaining dead ends.<br /> <br /> Finally, we're about...Oh, nearing the three year-mark I'd say. The quiet, thoughtful wallflower Twilight, whose been sweet on Viridian Strix like FOREVER without saying a word about it. (He'd totally friend-zoned her unconsciously) Just LOSES HER SHIT! The Limit Break fallout was epic, and pretty much rehabilitating the party's image in the minds of the people of the Domain that bears her name/she's the queen of took much of the next 12-13 sessions...Anyways, with that out of the way, and with not a drop of prior warning OOC from Lireal's player, we get in-game &quot;Eventide Seraph, you're going to have to cover for me at the capitol's Calibration festivities. I have....something important to take care of.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, you can imagine what's on the mind of the centuries-old Chosen of Secrets, and he correctly deduces what Lireal's planning. To his surprise, he gets nowhere with the normally agreeable, quiet Twilight. He wants to be there, but she's neatly trapped him as her second in the running of the Domain...so off he goes to handle politics, sweating bullets while the Twilight retires to summon Ligier.<br /> <br /> I swear, you could've heard a pin drop around the table. The IC tension created by Seraph tattling to the other party-members on Lireal morphed into OOC tension right-quick, because it was well-understood by then that Ligier is FURIOUS at this point about their persistent, determined, dedicated and most importantly, effective efforts to keep Strix on the straight-and-narrow (or as straight and narrow as a Slayer with a Malfean Urge gets). There's been quite a bit go down where his subtle and sometimes not-so-subtle machinations have been indicative of a progressive loss of patience with their interference, and now the Twilight wants to call Ligier up, bind him, and grill him on how to break Strix free of Hell forever. The context couldn't have been plainer that Ligier was going to rip their souls out and puke spit-pea soup down the holes in their Exaltations if he got loose if I'd spray-painted it on the wall. It also bears remembering that Ligier does not in fact HIMSELF know how this might be accomplished, as more than the vaguest theoretical.<br /> <br /> I've gotta say, hands-down, this was the most fun I'd ever had with anything Yozis-related in a game of Exalted. Dawn (Lireal's player) has brought her A-game, and she's doing this whole &quot;Trying to be big and bad, but really scared shitless&quot; schtick that's dead-on....So, up comes Ligier. He's so furious, he brought flash-cards made of malfean brass (with impeccable Old Realm calligraphy, of course), because he's <b>punctured his own ear-drums</b> while crossing Cecelyne. He isn't having any &quot;Even an offered deal the demon rejects makes it easier to bind.&quot; He's out for blood, and he's doing his absolute level-best to ensure Lireal can't offer such a deal before it's time to get to the clash of wills. Fortunately, Lireal just HAPPENED (and I mean this in the sense she'd asked the powerful Garda-bird she has a Celestine Pact with to be there, to help as combat-support if Ligier gets loose) to have a fire-elemental on hand. Thinking fast, she starts ordering the Garda-bird to burn her deal-terms into the wall behind her.<br /> <br /> Problem: The Garda-bird speaks, and can read Old Realm, but has never had cause to WRITE.<br /> Solution: The Twilight stunts teaching the Garda-bird to write on the spot. Legendary Scholar Curriculum + 1st Lore Excellency. I set the difficulty high (9). She's attempting to impart an entire body of knowledge, under pressure, to a sufficient complexity it qualifies as sorcerous bargaining during a demon-summoning rite. While the elemental in question is terrified almost beyond the capacity for rational thought. I give her two dice for the stunt.<br /> <br /> Int 5 + Lore 5 + 1 (I decide her demon-summoning Occult-specialty applies here) + (2) Stunt + 3 dice due to 1st Lore Excellency (She's already blown a healthy chunk on Summon Demon of the Third Circle, and she's trying to hold something back if Ligier gets loose. Like that's going to matter, hah)<br /> <br /> It was the first and only time I've ever seen more than four 10s result in any rolled die pool. She gets a couple successes, SIX 10s, and 3 of those rolled over into successes. 11 successes. The Garda bird has a migraine now, but it's been flash-prepared as a journeyman scribe, just about ready to leave its master and strike out as a fully-trained scribe. So here we have the Garda-bird burning Old Realm characters into the walls, the floor, eventually the ceiling...and boy is Ligier even madder at this turn of events.<br /> <br /> Dawn finally twigs to the fact Lireal's an Exalt-stain on Ligier's boots if he goes free, so she goes all in on dumping Essence into the clash. So, on top of everything, we've got a huge white-gold-and-sunset hued phoenix with a chained orichalcum tome in its claws raging in this underground summoning chamber from her anima blazing totemic (You can imagine Ligier is even, if that were possible by this point, MORE furious at the blazing anima in his face)<br /> <br /> Clash of wills. Now, she's managed to knock a -1 off trying to bargain and Ligier basically &quot;Haha, you've obviously lost your about-to-be-damned mind, Copper Spider, NO&quot; her, but here's where Lireal gets clever on me. She details how she's well-aware Ligier will go on a rampage if he gets loose. That once he's done with her, he's obviously going to go Exalt-hunting to squish the other Interventionists who've been relentless in keeping Viridian Strix from falling back into old habits, and how the ensuing battle will most assuredly devastate Sunset (the capitol of the Domain). Now, I handle Immanent Solar Glory and (for Lunars) Silver Lunar Resolution Charms a bit differently. I long ago ruled the Peripheral Essence gained can only be used on the same sort of focus by which said Essence can be regained, to prevent the Charms from being turned into simple Essence-pool-expanders. (I created two Charms that use these as prerequisites, with steeper requirements to do that, that go after these Charms in their trees)...Lireal doesn't have that one, but she's got Immanent Solar Glory, and she explains to me how this situation applies to her queenship, because Ligier is a direct, existential threat to the Domain's continued existence.<br /> <br /> Fortunately for her, the requirements are silent on the fact she's the one who CAUSED said direct, existential threat to be...but I find this both clever and in keeping with the Charm's intended purpose. She dumps the extra twenty motes (she bought it twice) into the binding-attempt....and ::drum roll:: Takes Ligier by one success. Kid you not, totemic anima, four peripheral motes to her name...and a murderously unhappy-but-bound Ligier to her name. It was everything I could've asked for in a first Third Circle Demon summoning. I'd kinda thought I woulda been jealous (none of the games I'VE gotten to play Exalted in have things progressed to the point of me having a sorcerer PC who could summon a Third Circle Demon), but I had a BLAST roleplaying Ligier. Even the sullen-but-drawing up what remained of his dignity about himself during the Q&amp;A which followed was great...<br /> <br /> Ligier's theoretical notions DID, after about another year, lead to the concrete knowledge Viridian Strix needed. More importantly, Lireal was so relentlessly exacting in her Q&amp;A, she managed to uncover the 150 year lifespan-limit that'd been put on the Infernals. (One of her Perception + Investigation rolls beat Ligier's Wits + Socialize, and she realized he was trying to hide something)...So ensued Viridian Strix's sudden burning interest in Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Edit: Linowan also had a bad Calibration, but that is an entirely different story <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","user":"Wyldwraith","date":". 07-25-2018, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T13:26:15-07:00","id":1238675,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day, it's the players that make a game great, and it sounds like you have some good ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T13:30:11-07:00","id":1238677,"title":"","content":"Current game I'm ST'ing - its a 2.5 ed. game, with a few extra homebrew rules, set in the South. All 4 players are engineering students and had never played the game before.<br /> <br /> 4 alchemicals (my hapless players) each manage to take just about three steps out of their vats for the first time, when they get plot-zapped to Creation.<br /> <br /> ...cue trying to figure out what the hell is going on, because they don't have that many memories of Autochtonia, nor do they have much of a clue of how or what Creation is.<br /> <br /> They meet some hesitant natives, turn them into friendly natives after showing what an iron hammer does to a bunch of fair folk and rescuing some kidnapped villagers, and then its off to the nearest big city.<br /> <br /> There they meet the Sultan, present the barely 'alive' remains of the fair folk lord they unknowingly stripped of graces during their fight. This earns them the Sultan's good will, granting them ownership of a particularly potent but similarly dangerous demense up in the nearby mountains.<br /> <br /> To construct their own vat complex manse there, they'll need cap-stones - who has those? Why, the realm does! Cue fun lil raiding party up north to Harborhead, where a realm legion is building manses because reasons.<br /> <br /> a bit of 'friendly' mind-control on nearby tribal chiefs starts a nice diversionary rebellion, giving the players room to make off with the cap-stones... or that would have happened, if not for one of the players being a prideful brawler who doesn't really do stealth, or the fact that assassinating the legion's commander made the legion's ranking immaculate monk (well, abbot) really mad and apparently he could actually fight back. This made the brawler and the rest of the players run off, luckily that was with the capstones - and they managed to avoid detection - allowing them to return 'home' with their booty... and with the knowledge that they are totally not the most powerful warriors or exalts around.<br /> <br /> Cue a time-skip for building a manse - which wasn't very long due to a friendly sorcerer they 'rescued' from the legion 'helping' by summoning demon workers. Only five babies nearly got killed because of that.<br /> <br /> with the vat-manse complex done the players blew most of their XP on attribute upgrades and new charms, plus they managed to get into contact with Autochtonia via a hack to the noetic charm network.<br /> <br /> ...and that's roughly where the game has reached so far<br /> <br /> up next is them being contracted by the Varangian city states to 'handle' a 'bandit king' known as &quot;Admiral Sand&quot; - he will of course give them a different offer, and they'll be meeting a 'villain' in the form of a fifth alchemical who has some very specific ideas of what should be done to Creation - and that alchy will of course demand the player's cooperation, otherwise its apostasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T13:59:58-07:00","id":1238684,"title":"","content":"My current 2.75 game is called A Nexus Minute, and involves four Solar PCs (Yoshiteru [Dawn], Xie Lan [Zenith], Whisper of Tarnished Silver [Night], and Abra, Mother of Nations [Eclipse]) and their Twilight NPC. they started relatively low-end on the goals - steal shit, gather the &quot;lost&quot; of Nexus, that sort of thing - but have currently amped up their goals to fighting the Walker in Darkness.<br /> <br /> To do this, they have found the mad scribblings of the Exalt Erebus, sole chosen of Nyx, brother to the Maidens, and are using it in a dark ritual to strip the Walker of his immortality. They have had to go to Stygia, Meru, and Yu-Shan to collect all the information they needed to perform the ritual. They even briefly met the Unconquered Sun! <br /> <br /> Next session will also be the last session, one way or another, as the armies of the Deathlord come crashing down on Nexus, and the ragtag &quot;army&quot; of the PCs has to band together to stop it, culminating in a five-on-one fight against the Walker, maybe the Green Lady, MAYBE EREBUS. They'll need to protect Xie Lan while she performs the ritual, then defeat the Walker and his array of near-perfect defenses, THEN use Ghost-Eating Technique on him to defeat his &quot;normal&quot; &quot;immortality,&quot; but the ritual will strip away any Neverborn-level protections on him and make him &quot;vulnerable.&quot; <br /> <br /> He's either going to die like a fish on land or net a TPK, I'm not sure which.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T15:17:09-07:00","id":1238703,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23907\" data-vbnamecard=\"23907\">Measure of Hope</a> Your modern-shard Abyssals game sounds like a blast. I always wanted to do something with Shards, but never had the right player-interest for it. I am wondering if Infernals see much use in other people's games, especially with regards to anything but Infernals &quot;played straight&quot; Ie: Mainly all Infernals, mainly all in collusion with Hell. I know a lot of people (including me) praise the creativity behind the Infernal Charm-set, but it seems like rogue Abyssals are a lot more popular than rogue or go-rogue-during-play Infernals. I was honestly shocked when Jacob wanted to play one in a mixed game. Jazzed, but definitely shocked.<br /> <br /> I will say, as a huge East fan (I set probably 90% of my games in either the Confederation area, Halta and points north or northeast, or the Hundred Kingdoms) the endless stalemate between Halta and Linowan seems odd to me. Especially with regards to the whole Bull of the North. Them leaving it at (reasons) to explain the Bull's withdrawal back North, after shredding the Talinin and Roka-Jin, and beating Linowan forces allied with the Tepet legions kind of made me go: &quot;Huh? What strategic goals, beyond making a mess, was the Bull trying to advance here?&quot; Beyond that, why the Haltans aren't fired up to finish off the weakened eternal enemy, that everyone knows isn't going to get anymore Realm help, triggers another &quot;Huh?&quot;<br /> <br /> Glad to see I'm not alone in using the Walker in Darkness as an antagonist regularly. He's just so well-situated for groups interested in protecting Nexus, but even more so Great Forks. I generally feel that despite the Mask having fired up active hostilities, the Walker would be on a lot of people's red-lists, with his utter death-zone of a territory right there, so central.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T22:45:11-07:00","id":1238796,"title":"","content":"I'd say rogue Infernals are more popular in 2e games than rogue Abyssals, because frankly they're more playable. I've seen two Infernals played, each for over a year, whereas the one rogue Abyssal lasted 3 sessions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T00:11:27-07:00","id":1239214,"title":"","content":"Hmm,<br /> Could be a case of my personal experience as a Storyteller, and the limited pool of Exalted players I get to talk to, that have biased my perception that rogue Infernals don't see much use. I really got fired up with inspiration for a campaign where everyone went from Chrysalis Grotesque end of preludes, through individual breaks with Hell (Even had plans as to how to handle it when only part of the group had broken away), but couldn't convince three of my four players it'd be fun. Sadly, one was utterly biased against Infernals by the horrid Lillun comic. The second was that player's husband, so he essentially backed her out of marital solidarity despite not having the same level of reaction to that puerile squick, and the third just doesn't like &quot;corrupted Solars&quot; and dislikes Abyssals even more than Infernals. They warmed some when Jacob did such an awesome job with his Infernal, but only in the context of admiring someone else's character/roleplaying <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The only other type of game I ever experienced such resistance to even the concept, was proposing a Circle of Sidereals. That one was a complete non-starter with three of four. I had more luck convincing the DB-haters to try a Dynast game, than convincing two of my people it wouldn't be &quot;dull&quot; playing Sidereals ( ::sighs:: )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T09:57:03-07:00","id":1239348,"title":"","content":"In all my years of playing/running Exalted (so, about 11?) I've only ever seen one Sidereal played for about 3 sessions. Which is a shame.<br /> <br /> But no, there was a phase where Infernals were all the rage; loads of cool charms, ideas, concepts. I was surprised to only see 2 rogue Infernals, tbh.<br /> <br /> (We also played a full Infernals game, but it didn't go very well, more I think because of the players than the ST or plot)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T14:14:33-07:00","id":1239435,"title":"","content":"Yeah,<br /> Infernal played straight, even with mature players, can get a bit grim. Like Abyssals, I think having a good ST is even more critical than usual. It's too easy to slide into levels of grimdark some part of the group won't be comfortable with, without someone with a deft, sensitive hand on the wheel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T06:22:12-07:00","id":1240006,"title":"","content":"So, my other campaign. I started running this at university when I was like 21, and 10 years later it's still going, though there were a couple of hiatuses. Recently, my friend has taken over, as I found running an Essence 5 game of Solars just too damn awkward (there were, at the time I stopped running it, no books beyond the Core and Miracles).<br /> It's a long game, so I might have got some chronology mixed up.<br /> <br /> Originally the group met in the Hundred Kingdoms. After some initial changes and deaths over the first story, the group settled into this:<br /> <b>Brasidas</b>, Dawn leader of a mercenary army<br /> <b>Dupree</b>, Twilight mad scientist<br /> <b>Thothmet</b>, one-eyed albino Eclipse sorcerer/necromancer<br /> <b>Prince del Fuego</b>, aristocratic casanova Eclipse followed by his faithful retainer, Bumbling Sage<br /> <b>I'chan</b>, Twilight Djala alchemist and archer on his mighty Tyrant Lizard, J'Quon.<br /> <b>Babar</b>, drunken Full Moon elephant-totem ex-Immaculate monk followed by his cult of nun-wives.<br /> <b>Timid Silk Blossom</b>, graceful rabbit-totem casteless and faithful member of the Cult of the Illuminated. Brasidas's Lunar mate (but her love was unrequited)<br /> <b>The Ebon Prince Clad in Savage Crimson</b>, deicidal Zenith from a desert monastery that worshipped the &quot;Old Masters&quot; and had a shadow-demon advisor, Zavis, the Black Flame.<br /> <br /> They wandered the Hundred Kingdoms, fighting an Abyssal circle serving Walker in Darkness, defeating a mad Dragonblood king, fighting the Wyld Hunt (and rescuing them from the mad King, who wanted to harvest the shikaris'... progenitive essence), and replacing hostile rulers with friendly ones.<br /> Babar disguised himself as Rabab, priest of Endings, and learnt kung-fu from a depressed Dynast, Cynis Danu. He then faked his own death at the hands of Babar the Anathema so as to motivate Danu to join the Wyld Hunt and make something of himself.<br /> Then they discovered that Ma-Ha-Suchi had invaded and razed Greyfalls, and was poised to invade the Hundred Kingdoms. They'd need to unite the Hundred Kingdoms to battle him.<br /> They went and asked the Confederation of Rivers for help, but the Confederation was too busy panicking over Walker in Darkness. They also met a rogue Abyssal, Murder of Crows, who became an occasional ally (with some unresolved sexual tension with Dupree).<br /> So the party said &quot;let's just go kill this Walker in Darkness chap, then they can help us fight Ma-Ha-Suchi.&quot;<br /> They dropped a superweapon on Walker in Darkness's army, defeating that force.<br /> <br /> Brasidas and Prince del Fuego stayed in the Hundred Kingdoms, while the others left. Timid took I'chan to the Cult of the Illuminated training camp for a bit, and he kind of semi-converted.<br /> <br /> Dupree, Thothmet, I'chan, Babar, Timid, and a new Lunar, Silver Shark, went to Great Forks next, but found that Ebon Prince and his Infernal mates were doing a rock concert devoted to Malfeas, which unleashed a massive slave revolt. The PCs took some slaves to freedom, leaving Ebon Prince.<br /> <br /> They then travelled west to Nexus, along with another rogue Abyssal, Silver Shark's mate. On the way, Cynis Danu tried to murder Babar at his wedding, but was driven off. They stopped by at the Cult headquarters to find everyone had been killed or kidnapped by Walker in Darkness. Also, Sidereals used Shun the Smiling Lady on Babar and all his wives left him.<br /> <br /> On the way (I think, can't remember exactly when this happened), the PCs were taken to Heaven for the Calibration party. Babar got thrown in prison for brawling. The others went to see the Unconquered Sun speak; but Lyta and some other Solars turned up and threw Chejop Kejak's head at his feet, saying they'd killed Kejak as a sacrifice to him. But he was not amused, had them arrested, and chose the PCs as their judges (this was actually a test to see if Solars could be fair when judging other Solars). The PCs had Lyta executed, and her accomplices Eclipse-task-bound to serve Heaven for a set number of tasks each.<br /> Then they returned to Creation.<br /> <br /> In Nexus they destroyed the Guild's headquarters, and had all their artefacts stolen by Harmonious Jade in revenge, fought some Immaculates, and helped Murder of Crows protect a mysterious coffin (it had Lytek in, but the PCs didn't know that) from Walker in Darkness. The Emissary also turned up, and Walker killed him, but Murder of Crows escaped with the coffin, and the PCs also escaped. Also, a god turned up and handed Silver Shark his son by Siakal.<br /> Shortly afterwards, the young shark-boy was kidnapped by an evil nanny who everyone knew was a Sidereal except Silver Shark.<br /> As they were leaving, Bronze Faction assassins tried to kill them. They incapacitated half the party, and killed Silver Shark's Abyssal mate (or so he thought; actually they just knocked her out and Timid stealthily killed her because she hated her). Most were driven off, but during the fight, I'chan limit broke and insisted on an honourable duel with the last Sidereal. He stabbed himself to make it fair. Babar was not cool with a hot chick being killed by I'chan, so hit him over the head to knock him out. But Babar's very strong, and I'chan's head went splat.<br /> <br /> Silver Shark stayed behind while the others went south, and met another group of Celestials who they joined up with.<br /> So the group was now:<br /> <b>Dupree</b>, sarcastic Twilight mad scientist-craftsman and doctor<br /> <b>Thothmet</b>, one-eyed albino Eclipse sorcerer/necromancer<br /> <b>Babar</b>, drunken Full Moon elephant-totem ex-Immaculate monk and Dupree's Lunar mate<br /> <b>Timid Silk Blossom</b>, graceful rabbit-totem casteless and faithful member of the Cult of the Illuminated<br /> <b>Janis, </b>octopus-totem Full Moon<br /> <b>Gentle Brook</b> , Night caste musician and Silver Nightingale master<br /> <b>Righteous Beacon of Unconquered Virtues</b>, Zenith priest and teacher<br /> <br /> They travelled south, to take I'chan's body back to the Djala jungle, having some minor adventures, and clashed with Walker's forces again. Also, Beacon and Babar both kept trying to seduce Timid, who was not interested (I'chan had also been in love with her, but backed off because he could see she needed to get over some issues first). They asked her parents for her hand, but the parents stayed non-committal. Also, it turned out some of Babar's ex-wives were spies for Mask of Winters, and others for Walker in Darkness.<br /> Silver Shark ate one of Babar's ex-wives, and the party hunted him down and butchered him.<br /> <br /> The party met Prince del Fuego again, who along with some ex-Cult Solars, had been turned into Abyssals. Babar agreed (and was Moonshadow-bound) to talk to them peacefully. Then killed del Fuego. This caused Babar's one last wife to die horribly.<br /> <br /> Then Dupree, Gentle Brook and Timid were kidnapped by Walker's remaining Abyssals, and taken to a tower in the Labyrinth. The Night was turned into an Abyssal, but Dupree managed to resist the power of the Monstrance long enough for Timid to free everyone and escape.<br /> However, when the Abyssals came to hunt them down, they grabbed Timid's dad and took him back. So the circle went to the Labyrinth to destroy the tower and kill the Abyssals. They won, but found Timid's dad had become an Abyssal, Tarnished Pariah.<br /> Also, as the party was killing the Abyssals, they saw Bumbling Sage, del Fuego's servant, escaping on a demon-wasp.<br /> Then Murder of Crows turned up with some friends to take all the Monstrances.<br /> <br /> Having left the tower in ruins and killed most of the Abyssals (except two who escaped), the now-Abyssal Gentle Brook begged the party to kill him, and they made Janis do it.<br /> <br /> So, finally the party was finished with all the Abyssal stuff (and received a congratulatory message from Mask of Winters for having wrecked Walker's forces) and carried on travelling south. Thothmet, however, went off to do his own magical things, take over a manse, and set up a large humanitarian charity across the Scavenger Lands.<br /> He later created his own race of three-eyed dragon men.<br /> <br /> The party was now:<br /> <b>Dupree</b>, <b>Master of Lunars and Butcher of Lookshy</b>, sarcastic Twilight mad scientist-craftsman and doctor<br /> <b>- </b>, Full Moon gecko-totem assassin (I can't remember his name)<br /> <b>Babar</b>, depressed Full Moon elephant-totem ex-Immaculate monk and necromancer, Dupree's Lunar mate, in love with both Beacon and Timid<br /> <b>Timid Silk Blossom</b>, traumatised rabbit-totem Casteless Lunar, motivated to become a fanatical killer in service of the Solars<br /> <b>Righteous Beacon of Unconquered Virtues</b>, Zenith priest and teacher, in love with Timid<br /> <b>I'chan</b>, Djala nemissary possessing his own corpse, with his ghost-tyrant lizard familiar J'quon<br /> <b>White Lion</b>, northern Full Moon warrior<br /> <br /> They went to the Djala jungle, and set up base in an old ziggurat-manse, built by Babar's previous incarnation.<br /> Timid met and fell in love with another Lunar, Lysa Bloody-Claws, and together with Dupree they went and healed many members of the Jackal Tribes to gain their help. Then they went to Varang, and began to cause trouble, manouevre, and rescue Djala, while the Lunar assassin murdered police-caste and soldier-castes. I'chan demanded &quot;let my people go!&quot; Eventually the government of Varang let all Djala return to the jungle, where I'chan was hailed as a national hero.<br /> <br /> Lysa had to leave, and without her, Timid was too depressed, and went into hibernation.<br /> <br /> Beacon and Babar got together, but Beacon was still in love with Timid. He went off to try stopping a war between Harborhead and Varang, by himself, introduced himself to some Dragonblood Dynasts, and they killed him.<br /> <br /> The rest of the party teamed up with a rogue Infernal Queen and had some adventures south of the jungle, fighting other Infernals, some Abyssals of Eye and Seven Despairs, etc.<br /> Dupree did a mighty experiment to create a genetic virus that would change humanity so everyone would have Exalted Healing and Enlightened Essence, and unleashed it to slowly spread across Creation.<br /> (However, later the Sidereals stopped it, though it did change all the Djala, and random other people)<br /> <br /> But then they learnt that Walker in Darkness, and his two lieutenants (one of whom had destroyed Lookshy while disguised as Dupree) were planning to destroy the world using the Realm Defence Grid. They chased his lieutenant through the Labyrinth and killed him, then carried on to Stygia.<br /> <br /> So the party was:<br /> <b>Dupree</b>, <b>Master of Lunars and Butcher of Lookshy</b>, sarcastic Twilight mad scientist-craftsman and doctor<br /> <b>Babar</b>, depressed Full Moon elephant-totem ex-Immaculate monk and necromancer, Dupree's Lunar mate<br /> <b>The Northerner</b>, Night caste thief<br /> <b>Mara</b>, Slayer, cult leader, and queen of Irem of the Pillars<br /> <b>Virtuous Viper</b>, snake-totem Full Moon and Robin Hood-esque bandit<br /> <br /> They left Stygia for the Imperial City, watched the Palace of the Anathema, and saw Walker in Darkness and some Abyssals appear and fight their way inside.<br /> The PCs followed, fighting/sneaking past various traps.<br /> They fought some Abyssals, and defeated them, but the Northerner took an arrow in the face then fell 100 foot and died.<br /> <br /> They reached the antechamber to the Panoptican Apocalyptic, and discovered a whole bunch of dead Sidereals. Only one, Red Rust, who they knew previously, survived. He explained that they'd been betrayed by Sidereal Akuma of the Ebon Dragon. He also had several potions of Rune of Singular Hate, made in the Crucible of Tarim.<br /> <br /> The PCs reached the control room, finding Walker in Darkness feeding his last Abyssal (one of the ones Timid had once known in the Cult training camp) to the Sword of Creation to gain control of it. The PCs attacked... and he killed Virtuous Viper (an Essence 5 Full Moon) in one round.<br /> Mara, Babar and Red Rust all used Rune of Singular Hate on Walker, and he exploded.<br /> <br /> The PCs began to fight over what to do with the Sword of Creation. Babar used it to destroy all entrances to Yu-Shan with the World-Denying Solipsism Protocol, and Dupree shot it at the Wyld a lot.<br /> But Murder of Crows, Ledaal Kes, Ragara Szaya, Nellens Poromo and the Prophet of Falling Stars (who they'd heard of as a servant of the First and Forsaken Lion previously) turned up. The Prophet of Falling Stars revealed himself as the ghost of Chejop Kejak. He explained that Murder of Crows' master Mask of Winters (she'd been lying about being a rogue), the First and Forsaken Lion, Eye of Seven Despairs, and the ghost of the Scarlet Empress had teamed up with him to put the Neverborn to sleep by, among other things, severing the Underworld from Creation using the Sword of Creation combined with Void-Circle workings. To do so, of course, would involve killing everyone who lived in a shadowland, but he considered that a small price to pay.<br /> Babar did not, and a fight ensued.<br /> <br /> By the end, only Babar was standing (with the unconscious ghost of Kejak inside him), with everyone else either dead or unconscious, except a servant. Who revealed himself as Bumbling Sage, Fiend of the Ebon Dragon. Babar grabbed Mara and Dupree, and fled through a broken Portal of Infinite Passage.<br /> This left Kes to wake up, kill the unconscious Poromo, use the Sword of Creation to destroy a bunch of Shadowlands (but not all), and declare himself the Azure Emperor.<br /> <br /> And that was the end of the game.<br /> <br /> I continued in 3rd ed, but I'll write that up later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-29-2018, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T07:59:53-07:00","id":1240051,"title":"","content":"So, 25 years later (including 1 year of eternal night, one war in Yu-Shan, a second Balorian Crusade, a Lunar invasion of the Realm, the destruction of the Loom of Fate and a new one being built by the returned Authocthon, and V'neef seizing the throne from Kes and killing Mnemon and Ragara)...<br /> <br /> A wandering hero, Princess Enhenduanna, exiled sorcerer-princess of Sippar, was travelling through the Djala jungle. She was hired by the Chancellor, Princess T'chan. It seems the Princess's husband, I'chan, Deathlord of the Djala, had been kidnapped by martial artists using an evil ghost-prison box.<br /> According to the Djala oracle, Enhenduanna would have to form a band of legendary heroes to rescue I'chan!<br /> So, Enhenduanna managed to find a couple of Solars, then journeyed to a hidden village of Illuminated beastmen ninja-missionaries and convinced an old friend of I'chan to come out of retirement to help.<br /> Then they travelled to a cursed manse in a swamp protected by demons. There they found two ancient heroes trapped in amber and cut them out (there was a third amber prison... which had already been opened).<br /> <br /> So the PCs were:<br /> <b>Princess Enhenduanna</b>, exiled sorceress of a desert kingdom, pact-bound with Adramelch, a forbidden god of sacrificial fire (Eclipse)<br /> <b>River Glow</b>, author and intellectual, and an old friend of I'chan (Eclipse)<br /> <b>Timid Silk Blossom</b>, rabbit-Lunar and goddess of the hidden village. Mostly sane. (Casteless)<br /> <b>Reborn in Shining Light</b>, head priest of the Cult of the Illuminated bandit village of Hen Ling (Zenith)<br /> <b>Dupree</b>, legendary hero/monster swordsman/doctor/craftsman who's been slumbering for 25 years. Sidereals hate him because he gave all Djala Exalted healing and extended lifespan. (Twilight)<br /> <b>Babar</b>, legendary hero/monster who's been slumbering for 25 years. Still not over Beacon. (Full Moon)<br /> <br /> The heroes travelled north and tracked down the mercenary martial artists, and learnt that they'd been hired by Chakravatri, Queen of the Underworld, a necromancer/crime-boss and member of the Ascended, a sorcerous coven. But Timid killed a prisoner, which infuriated River Glow.<br /> So next the PCs tracked her down. She turned out to be one of the Dragonblood rulers of Varamaya, a kingdom north of Hen Ling. Enhenduanna (pretending to be a Fire Aspect from House Sesus) killed her. But the party discovered she'd given I'chan to her coven-member Moku Star-Spear, court sorcerer of the Leopard Empire (Harborhead, Varang, some other small places). He intended to use I'chan as part of a working to raise all the Djala ghosts in Varang to use against the Realm.<br /> <br /> The party travelled to Kirighast to investigate Moku. Different party members tried different tactics to catch Moku, which led to further tension.<br /> Eventually, they caught and killed Moku and his apprentice and rescued I'chan. Then they took him back to his capital, but River Glow left.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They chilled for a bit with I'chan at his capital, but discovered that I'chan had been bound by some guy called the Leper Prince, who made I'chan come and report to him annually and secretly.<br /> So they chased him to a town south of the jungle, where he and his friend the Cardinal of the Cathedral Encarmine were torturing suspected demon cultists for the King.<br /> The PCs fought them, killing the Leper Prince and capturing the Cardinal. But there was a lot of flaring. Also Timid grabbed the King and ran off with him to the forest.<br /> The King was enamoured of Timid and decided to ally with the group. The others tortured the Cardinal and then let him go. They learnt he was a member of the Crimson Masters, a Celestial circle who led a barbarian horde.<br /> <br /> The circle then celebrated with the King at a big party, but some Immaculates turned up and accused Dupree of being the infamous demon-sorcerer Dupree, Butcher of Lookshy. Dupree was thrown in prison. He easily escaped though.<br /> <br /> A couple of Dragonblood relatives of the Queen turned up, princes from nearby kingdoms. They seemed to get on well with the PCs... but then the PCs realised the Dragonblood had called in the Wyld Hunt to ambush them!<br /> The circle ambushed the Wyld Hunt instead, killing half of them, but their leader, Cynis Danu, Babar's frenemy, escaped with his lieutenant. The PCs also killed the Queen and her relatives.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They then established the King, Aquos Daanadsson (he was an undersea mutant faking being a Water Aspect) as their puppet ruler, and spent some time doing stuff in his kingdom.<br /> <br /> They were politically outmanoeuvred by the neighbouring Queen, Ashen Witch, however, (also, she seduced Babar. It's not difficult) and Aquos agreed to marry her (so she'd expand her control).<br /> But Enhenduanna was able to convince some local tribesmen (with her dragons) to come to the mountains with her as their queen, so she could create a new magical kingdom.<br /> <br /> Then they met their old friend/enemy Ebon Prince, who took them to a manse he'd been stuck in in the nearby mountains. It had a demon library in, and a bound behemoth. Enhenduanna later sent elemental guards and people to learn from the demon library so they could become bureaucrats for her new kingdom.<br /> <br /> Then at Ashen Witch's wedding, they met the Godslayer, the Eclipse of the Crimson Masters, who'd come to negotiate peace. They killed him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The PCs were now:<br /> <b>Queen Enhenduanna</b>, dragon-riding sorceress and ruler of the new mountain kingdom of H'hui'shan (Eclipse)<br /> <b>Fulgens Cruciatus</b>, warmaster of the Djala and fanatical follower of I'chan (Dawn)<br /> <b>Timid Silk Blossom</b>, beautiful swordswoman and fanatical devotee of the Cult of the Illuminated. (Casteless)<br /> <b>Reborn in Shining Light</b>, head priest of the Cult of the Illuminated bandit village of Hen Ling (Zenith)<br /> <b>Dupree</b>, sarcastic swordsman/doctor/craftsman (Twilight)<br /> <b>Babar</b>, debauched martial artist and necromancer (Full Moon)<br /> <b>Loyal Fox,</b> anarcho-feminist revolutionary (Eclipse)<br /> <br /> They then went south to take control of the city of Fakel, which was between Aquos's kingdom and the Crimson Horde, who broke off their war against a Realm satrapy and an army of locust-men (some kind of beastman, presumably).<br /> While there, they met two Sidereals; Sun Kong, monkey beastwoman and Babar's daughter (you don't want to know who her mother was) and Swims-Through-Stars, son of Siakal and Silver Shark (that's why Sidereals kidnapped him as a baby).<br /> There was a brutal campaign combining armies and magic against the Crimson Masters. Whole armies were destroyed, Fakel was wrecked, and several PCs were badly injured, but none died, and several Crimson Masters did.<br /> <br /> Afterwards, Enhenduanna returned to her mountain kingdom to continue magically improving it and consolidate her political control, Light and Loyal Fox stayed in Fakel to fix and run it on behalf of King Babar, and the others returned to I'chan's temple-city.<br /> <br /> There, they initiated a series of purges, show-trials, etc, in order to get rid of all the priests and nobles who opposed them politically, and continue their project to turn the tribes of the Djala jungle into a modern, centralised state, with bureaucrats and tax collectors and so on, devoted to I'chan as supreme god (I'chan himself's not that bothered). They did this with the help of Southern King and general evil suck-up Jin the Just.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then Babar and Timid went to see that manse with the demon library. And blew it up so Enhenduanna couldn't use it. This spewed lava everywhere, unleashed demons, distorted time, and freed the behemoth, who proceeded to go off and rampage around Harborhead.<br /> <br /> <br /> Babar and Timid next went to visit the Underworld, as they got a message from the First and Forsaken Lion's local Viceroy... Tarnished Pariah, Timid's dad.<br /> They went to his city, and stayed in his castle, with him and Timid's new step-mum, Murder of Crows. He told them he'd crushed the Crimson Horde in the Underworld, but some of the Crimson Masters can come back to life.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Fulgens continued taking brutal control of the Djala, putting himself on the council with the 4 directional Djala kings and Timid's puppet high priest. There was a rebellion, but it was defeated.<br /> <br /> At the same time, Dupree created a magical artefact that transformed I'chan from a ghost into an actual god.<br /> <br /> Timid and Babar decided to go speak to Tarnished Pariah's boss, the First and Forsaken Lion. He was very interested to meet Timid, as she was the reincarnation of his old Lunar mate. But he told his guards to kill Timid, so she could show off her stabbing skills, and Babar panicked, grabbed Timid, and jumped back to Creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Most of the PCs now returned to I'chan-city (built by Dupree) for a feast, but the remaining Crimson Masters plunged the temple into the Underworld and sent an army of ghosts (including the ghosts of Solars) at them. The PCs survived, but had to tromp to a Shadowland and back.<br /> <br /> However, when they returned, the Goddess of the Djala appeared and said I'chan was being promoted to Yu-Shan. She also commended Jin the Just for his piety.<br /> This of course, was all a plan of Jin the Just to get the PCs out of the jungle because he was fed up with their interference (in his plan to become supreme ruler of the Djala) and hoped without I'chan around, his friends would have now power, being non-Djala.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Later, Light got a message about Djala slaves being held by a merchant in Kirighast. He went off to rescue them, but was still wanted for involvement in the murder of the Imperatrix's court wizard, and so was arrested.<br /> The other PCs went to rescue both him and the Djala.<br /> Fulgens went to the merchant's house, where it turned out that the merchant was working for Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the others went to rescue Light (I rolled randomly, and they turned up just as he was being brought out onto the block). They found that the Imperatrix had several guests; the surviving Crimson Masters!<br /> The PCs attacked, but without their Dawn, as he'd been distracted by Sidereals.<br /> They won, finally defeating the Crimson Masters, but Light lost an arm. In the following fights, trying to defeat all the Imperatrix's other allies, Timid was knocked out, and Ahlat and 100 war-gods ambushed the PCs. Babar was permanently blinded by a burning spear to the face, and they lost track of Dupree.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Eventually, everyone escaped and met back at I'chan's capital. They realised Bronze-faction Sidereals and Ledaal Kes had manipulated the whole thing so as to pit the Realm's enemies against each other, ready for Ledaal Kes's legion to attack later. Babar decided to leave so as not to attract the Realm to the Djala jungle. But once he was gone, Jin the Just announced that the council had exiled and driven out the evil debauched sorcerer Babar. Babar was so insulted that he came back and killed Jin, throwing Djala politics into turmoil again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-29-2018, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T08:14:57-07:00","id":1240055,"title":"","content":"So, it's now over a year later. Light has called a big meeting of Solars to talk about re-establishing the Cult of the Illuminated in the South (Kether Rock was destroyed in the second Balorian crusade).<br /> <br /> The PCs are:<br /> <b>Queen Enhenduanna</b>, dragon-riding sorceress and ruler of the magical mountain kingdom of H'hui'shan (Eclipse)<br /> <b>Fulgens Cruciatus</b>, warmaster of the Djala and fanatical follower of I'chan (Dawn)<br /> <b>Timid Silk Blossom</b>, beautiful swordswoman and fanatical devotee of the Cult of the Illuminated. (Casteless)<br /> <b>Reborn in Shining Light</b>, head priest of the Cult of the Illuminated bandit village of Hen Ling (Zenith)<br /> <b>Loyal Fox,</b> revolutionary allied with the Cult of the Illuminated (Eclipse)<br /> <b>Golden Hero</b>, revolutionary who's come from the Sequestered Tabernacle to help fight the Realm. (Night)<br /> <br /> There's also two other Solars who came to see Light, King Elf-Wise (based on Alfred the Great) and Obsidian Butterfly (raised by Dragon Kings).<br /> <br /> The Leopard Imperium, the Realm and Varamaya have put aside their differences and united... against the PCs.<br /> But, at the same time, the Djala and the people of H'hui'shan have come into conflict as they're both trying to take control of the nearby lakes. So Fulgens and Enhenduanna were ready for war.<br /> <br /> Thus, the first few sessions were a peace conference. But then we discovered insane murderers on both sides with markings in Clawspeak. We went to Fakel to speak to King Babar, who told Timid to go to the town of Roses, which some Lunars had mysteriously visited.<br /> <br /> On the way, Fulgens and Enhenduanna decided to make peace.<br /> <br /> While reclining in some hot springs, we were ambushed by cultists who believed they'd been ordered to by the Leopard God. This turned out to be connected to a mysterious woman who'd also freed a number of Moonsilver tupplas made of traumatic first-age memories Lunars had got rid of, from their prison. I'm pretty sure she's a Sidereal trying to distract us from the impending Realm invasion.<br /> <br /> We returned north to announce peace, but the peace deal fell apart and Fulgens declared war on Enhenduanna's mountain kingdom. Obsidian Butterfly challenged him to a duel, but the others convinced her to put it off. I tried killing him, failed, Enhenduanna hit him with a Death Ray, he survived.<br /> <br /> So everyone has given up on making peace. The Cult members are off trying to stop the moonsilver serial killers and spy on nearby nations to find out when the invasion will happen and where.<br /> Fulgens and Enhenduanna are at war. Which means they'll be vulnerable to the two Realm legions and army of Prasadi auxiliaries that'll attack in a few months.<br /> <br /> And that's where we are now.<br /> <br /> Essentially, I think this is what happens when you have a set of Essence 5 Solars. Each has their own ideas about how to deal with things, and the power to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}